                <pb facs="0306" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg236"/>

                <head>No. 104.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scruggs to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18, 1883</date>.
                        (Received May 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 82.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For the information of the Department
                    [inclose herewith a copy; and translation of a convention of arbitration between
                    Colombia and Salvador, dated in Paris, December 24, 1880. You will observe that
                    the exchange of ratifications took place in Paris only on the 7th of January,
                    1882, and that whilst the Colombian President’s official proclamation of this
                    treaty is dated May 23, 1882, its publication was delayed until the 9th instant;
                    that is to say, fifteen months after the formal exchange of ratifications, and
                    nearly four months after President Zaldúa’s death. It is noticeable,
                    furthermore, that this treaty is substantially the same which Colombia sought to
                    make with Guatemala in December, 1881; the only difference being that, in the
                    last named, nothing is said about the proposed Panama congress, while the blank
                    in the corresponding second article of the Paris convention is filled by the
                    words the President of the United States of America.”</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM L. SCRUGGS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
            </div>
